  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\nIssued at 129 PM CDT MON JUL 27 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging shifts east through the work week, setting\nthe stage for significant heat risk. Tuesday stands out as the\nhottest and most oppressive day, with highs reaching the upper\n90s to near 100 degrees. Combined with dew points in the mid- to\nupper 70s, heat indices will approach 110. A Heat Advisory has\nbeen issued, beginning this afternoon for western areas and\nexpanding area-wide through Tuesday. While the MCS train\npersists, the primary track appears to remain east of our area on\nTuesday, limiting rain chances. However, rounds of showers and\nstorms remain possible as shortwave energy rotates along the\nridge's periphery. By mid-week, the ridge suppresses as a trough\nbuilds over the East Coast and a deep low develops over New\nEngland. This pattern change will allow for a gradual cooldown,\nwith highs trending into the upper 80s and low 90s by Friday.\n\n16",
